"use strict";(Array.isArray(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs)?self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs:self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=[]).push([[3037],{17228(e,t,i){i.r(t),i.d(t,{comp:()=>n,data:()=>a});var o=i(20641);const r={},n=(0,i(66262).A)(r,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,o.uX)(),(0,o.CE)("div",null,t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,o.Fv)('<h1 id="ai-usage-limits" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#ai-usage-limits"><span>AI Usage Limits</span></a></h1><p>Every request a vendor makes to Generative AI (Magic AI) consumes one generation from their allocated balance. Marketplace administrators have comprehensive controls to define global quota allowances, configure custom per-seller limits, select reset cycles, and monitor token consumption to keep platform costs predictable.</p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Budget Protection</p><p>Setting usage limits protects marketplace owners from unexpected third-party API bills while still giving vendors sufficient capacity to list and refresh their product catalogs quickly.</p></div><hr><h2 id="how-generations-are-counted" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-generations-are-counted"><span>How Generations Are Counted</span></a></h2><p>Magic AI tracks vendor usage using clear, intuitive rules:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Product Generation</strong>: Clicking <strong>Generate</strong> runs a full analysis across title, descriptions, specs, and SEO fields, consuming exactly <strong>1 generation</strong>.</li><li><strong>Single-Field Regeneration</strong>: Clicking the inline <strong>Regenerate</strong> button beside an individual field (e.g. asking for a different short description) consumes <strong>1 generation</strong>.</li><li><strong>Failed or Dropped Requests</strong>: If a third-party AI service is temporarily unavailable or returns an error, the request is <strong>not counted</strong> against the vendor&#39;s balance.</li><li><strong>Concurrent Limits</strong>: A vendor can run one active generation at a time to prevent duplicate concurrent API requests.</li><li><strong>Reset Schedule</strong>: Generation counts automatically reset to zero at midnight (for <strong>Daily</strong> limits) or on the 1st of each calendar month at 00:00 UTC (for <strong>Monthly</strong> limits).</li></ul><hr><h2 id="setting-global-limits-for-all-vendors" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#setting-global-limits-for-all-vendors"><span>Setting Global Limits for All Vendors</span></a></h2><p>Marketplace administrators can configure global quota policies under <strong>WordPress Admin &gt;&gt; WooCommerce Marketplace &gt;&gt; Settings &gt;&gt; Generative AI</strong>:</p><ol><li><strong>Per-Seller Limit</strong>: Enter the maximum number of AI generations permitted per seller within each period (e.g., <code>50</code>).</li><li><strong>Limit Period</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Daily</strong>: Best for continuous, steady inventory creation.</li><li><strong>Weekly</strong>: Suitable for moderate catalog expansion.</li><li><strong>Monthly</strong>: Recommended standard for marketplace operations.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Unlimited Generations</strong>: Leave the limit field blank or enter <code>0</code> to grant unrestricted AI generations to all sellers.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="customizing-limits-for-individual-vendors" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#customizing-limits-for-individual-vendors"><span>Customizing Limits for Individual Vendors</span></a></h2><p>Administrators can override global limits for specific merchants to reward high-volume sellers, support VIP vendors, or accommodate newly onboarded partners:</p><ol><li>Navigate to <strong>WordPress Admin &gt;&gt; Marketplace &gt;&gt; Vendors</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Edit</strong> on the target vendor account.</li><li>Scroll down to the <strong>Generative AI Settings</strong> section: <ul><li><strong>Inherit Global</strong>: Uses the marketplace-wide default quota.</li><li><strong>Custom Quota</strong>: Enter a bespoke generation allowance (e.g., <code>200</code> generations/month).</li><li><strong>Disable AI Access</strong>: Toggle off AI generation completely for flagged, suspended, or unverified seller accounts.</li></ul></li><li>Save the vendor profile to apply the change immediately.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="what-vendors-see" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#what-vendors-see"><span>What Vendors See</span></a></h2><p>Vendors always have full visibility over their remaining AI quota directly inside their dashboard:</p><ul><li><strong>Live Balance Meter</strong>: The Magic AI modal displays a clear counter showing remaining generations (e.g., <code>Generations remaining: 42 of 50 this month</code>).</li><li><strong>Low-Balance Warning</strong>: When a vendor reaches 5 or fewer remaining generations, the meter highlights in amber to warn them that their quota is almost exhausted.</li><li><strong>Quota Exceeded Notice</strong>: When the limit is reached, the generate button is temporarily disabled, and an informative notice explains when the quota will reset: <blockquote><p><em>&quot;You have reached your AI generation limit for this month. Your quota will automatically reset on the 1st of next month.&quot;</em></p></blockquote></li></ul><hr><h2 id="administrator-best-practices" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#administrator-best-practices"><span>Administrator Best Practices</span></a></h2><ul><li><strong>Start with a Baseline</strong>: A default allowance of 30 to 50 generations per month is typically sufficient for most active merchants while keeping API costs minimal (often under $0.05–$0.15 per vendor per month on models like GPT-4o-mini or Gemini 1.5 Flash).</li><li><strong>Offer Tiered Quotas</strong>: If you charge vendor subscription fees or use vendor tiers, bundle higher AI generation limits into premium vendor membership plans.</li><li><strong>Consider Local Ollama</strong>: For marketplaces with high catalog volume, consider deploying a private, self-hosted Ollama instance (such as Llama 3 or Mistral) to provide completely free, unlimited AI generation with zero third-party token costs.</li><li><strong>Monitor Third-Party Dashboards</strong>: Regularly review your OpenAI, Google AI Studio, or Anthropic developer consoles to track token consumption and configure hard billing caps on the provider side.</li></ul>',22)]))}]]),a=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/usage-limits.html","title":"AI Usage Limits","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"How Generations Are Counted","slug":"how-generations-are-counted","link":"#how-generations-are-counted","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Setting Global Limits for All Vendors","slug":"setting-global-limits-for-all-vendors","link":"#setting-global-limits-for-all-vendors","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Customizing Limits for Individual Vendors","slug":"customizing-limits-for-individual-vendors","link":"#customizing-limits-for-individual-vendors","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"What Vendors See","slug":"what-vendors-see","link":"#what-vendors-see","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Administrator Best Practices","slug":"administrator-best-practices","link":"#administrator-best-practices","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/usage-limits.md"}')}}]);